    </section>

    <!-- Main Content -->
    <main class="py-14 px-6 lg:px-8">
        <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto">

            <!-- Introduction -->
            <div class="bg-black/70 border border-gray-800 rounded-xl p-8 mb-14 shadow-lg">
                <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-black text-white mb-5">Hey Mama Llama,</h2>
                <p class="text-lg text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
                    Just checking in with an update on your plan. I've been thinking about the best way to structure your "homework" to complement the great work you're already doing with your Peloton and other activities.
                </p>
                <p class="mt-5 text-lg text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
                    Instead of just adding more of the same, I'm shifting our focus entirely. We're going to target the specific areas your current system isn't hitting. This is the smart approach to building a truly balanced and resilient body.
                </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Focus Areas Section -->
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-10">

                <!-- Focus Area 1 -->
                <div class="bg-black/70 border border-gray-800 rounded-xl p-8 flex flex-col hover:shadow-xl hover:shadow-electric-yellow/10 transition">
                    <div class="w-16 h-16 rounded-lg icon-container flex items-center justify-center mb-5">
                        <svg class="w-8 h-8 text-electric-yellow" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="currentColor">
                            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M11.48 3.499a.562.562 0 011.04 0l2.125 5.111a.563.563 0 00.475.345h5.364c.518 0 .734.654.372 1.01l-4.36 3.162a.563.563 0 00-.182.557l1.636 4.892c.164.492-.421.928-.848.597L12 18.348l-4.506 3.267c-.427.33-.014.105-.848-.597l1.636-4.892a.563.563 0 00-.182-.557l-4.36-3.162c-.362-.356-.146-1.01.372-1.01h5.364a.563.563 0 00.475-.345L11.48 3.5z"></path>
                        </svg>
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="text-2xl font-black text-electric-yellow">Focus 1: Reactivating Your Core</h3>
                    <p class="mt-4 text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
                        You highlighted your core as a weak spot. As I said on Tuesday, it's not weak at all—it's strong, just de-conditioned. It hasn't been challenged with the intensity we used to. Our first mission is to wake it up and get it firing properly again.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <!-- Focus Area 2 -->
                <div class="bg-black/70 border border-gray-800 rounded-xl p-8 flex flex-col hover:shadow-xl hover:shadow-electric-yellow/10 transition">
                    <div class="w-16 h-16 rounded-lg icon-container flex items-center justify-center mb-5">
                        <svg class="w-8 h-8 text-electric-yellow" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="currentColor">
                            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"></path>
                            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 9.563C9 9.252 9.252 9 9.563 9h4.874c.311 0 .563.252.563.563v4.874c0 .311-.252.563-.563.563H9.563A.562.562 0 019 14.437V9.564z"></path>
                        </svg>
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="text-2xl font-black text-electric-yellow">Focus 2: Confident Movement</h3>
                    <p class="mt-4 text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
                        Mobility isn't just about flexibility; it's about having <span class="font-bold text-white">confidence</span> in your movements. Your old injury has created a mental barrier around your left leg, which is completely normal.
                    </p>
                    <p class="mt-4 text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
                        If we don't actively train this out, that anxiety can grow and create a mental "no-go zone." This can lead to avoidance of the issue and, worse, that same anxiety can latch on much easier to any new injuries.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <!-- Focus Area 3 -->
                <div class="bg-black/70 border border-gray-800 rounded-xl p-8 flex flex-col hover:shadow-xl hover:shadow-electric-yellow/10 transition">
                    <div class="w-16 h-16 rounded-lg icon-container flex items-center justify-center mb-5">
                        <svg class="w-8 h-8 text-electric-yellow" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="currentColor">
                            <circle cx="12" cy="7" r="2"></circle>
                            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 9v4m0 0l-3 4m3-4l3 4m-6 0H7m8 0h2"></path>
                        </svg>
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="text-2xl font-black text-electric-yellow">Focus 3: Reclaiming Your Squat</h3>
                    <p class="mt-4 text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
                        Your Peloton and running have built fantastic leg strength, but they do so in a narrow range. Over time, if your knees aren't taken through a full squat pattern, the natural movement lessens.
                    </p>
                    <p class="mt-4 text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
                        This can force other areas to compensate, leading to flare-ups. Our goal is to re-teach this full-range pattern to build a more supple and movement-efficient foundation.
                    </p>
                </div>

            </div>

            <!-- The Goal Section -->
            <div class="mt-14 text-center">
                 <div class="inline-block bg-electric-yellow text-black font-bold uppercase tracking-widest py-2 px-6 rounded-full">
                    The Goal
                </div>
                <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl mx-auto text-xl sm:text-2xl text-gray-200 leading-relaxed">
